    "q-166217": {
      "dom_id": "question-166217",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "If we attempt to evaluate the limit directly by substituting $x=2,$ we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{4-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}}{4-{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since there is a radical in the numerator, we can evaluate the limit by first multiplying the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{4-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{(\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x})(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})}{(4-{x}^{2})(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{2-x}{(2+x)(2-x)(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\cancel{2-x}}{(2+x)\\cancel{(2-x)}(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{1}{(2+x)(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(2+2)(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4(2\\sqrt{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
