    "q-166218": {
      "dom_id": "question-166218",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The instantaneous rate of change of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ is given by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(2)={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{f(x)-f(2)}{x-2}=-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x\\,+$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$).$",
      "worked_solution": "Simplifying the expression under the limit, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(2) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{f(x)-f(2)}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{[4-{x}^{2}]-[4-{2}^{2}]}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{4-{x}^{2}}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{-({x}^{2}-4)}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{-(x+2)(x-2)}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{-(x+2)\\cancel{(x-2)}}{\\cancel{x-2}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
