    "q-166220": {
      "dom_id": "question-166220",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The derivative of $f(x)$ is defined by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$-\\,h\\,).$",
      "worked_solution": "Simplifying the expression under the limit, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{4-(x+h)^{2}-[4-{x}^{2}]}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{4-{x}^{2}-2xh-{h}^{2}-4+{x}^{2}}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{-2xh-{h}^{2}}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{h(-2x-h)}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{\\cancel{h}(-2x-h)}{\\cancel{h}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}(-2x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
